`chrome.enterprise.reportingPrivate.getContextInfo()` answers with the device's context again (#1088). Builds
without cloud content analysis (Helium's and ungoogled's: `enterprise_cloud_content_analysis=false`) answered with
no arguments, so callers got `undefined` and no `lastError`: Google's Endpoint Verification read
`realtimeUrlCheckMode` from it, threw and never reported the device, which kept context-aware access blocked.
`ContextInfoFetcher` already leaves the connector fields out in such builds, so it now runs in every build:
affiliation ids, browser version, site isolation, the built-in DNS client, Chrome Remote Desktop blocking, the OS
firewall and DNS servers, with real-time URL checks reported as disabled.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/enterprise_reporting_private/enterprise_reporting_private_api.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/enterprise_reporting_private/enterprise_reporting_private_api.cc
@@ -577,7 +577,6 @@
 
 ExtensionFunction::ResponseAction
 EnterpriseReportingPrivateGetContextInfoFunction::Run() {
-#if BUILDFLAG(ENTERPRISE_CLOUD_CONTENT_ANALYSIS)
   auto* connectors_service =
       enterprise_connectors::ConnectorsServiceFactory::GetInstance()
           ->GetForBrowserContext(browser_context());
@@ -591,9 +590,6 @@
       this));
 
   return RespondLater();
-#else
-  return RespondNow(NoArguments());
-#endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENTERPRISE_CLOUD_CONTENT_ANALYSIS)
